  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A mass-spring system undergoes simple harmonic motion on a horizontal, frictionless surface. The graph below shows the variation with time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> in seconds (s) of the displacement <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span> in centimetres (cm) of the mass from its equilibrium position.</p><p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> </p>Determine the period of the oscillation from the graph.<p>[1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> </p>Calculate the frequency of the oscillation.<p>[1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> </p>Calculate the magnitude of the maximum acceleration of the mass.<p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> </p>Identify whether the velocity of the mass is zero or at a maximum at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 1.0\\ \\mathrm{s}\"></span>. Justify your answer.<p>[2]</p></section>"
  },
